ield of a pulse of light of that length in $u$ along the axis, carrying the same energy $E$.","caption":["The plane of $u$ and $v$ ($x = \\rho_0/32$, $y = 0$), at distance $\\rho = \\rho_0/32$ from the axis the source moves along, drawn with $z = (v - u)/2$ and $ct = (u + v)/2$. Off the shock $u = 0$ the metric on this plane is $-du\\,dv$, flat, and light runs at 45°. The rays moving right keep their $u$ and run beside the shock without crossing it. Each ray moving left crosses it and comes out moved along it by $\\Delta v = -(8GE/c^4)\\ln(\\rho/\\rho_0) = (8GE/c^4)\\ln 32$, a delay of $(4GE/c^4)\\ln 32$ in $ct$.","The Christoffel symbol $\\Gamma^x{}_{uu}$ turns every light ray crossing the shock toward the axis, out of this plane, so the curves drawn are null curves, and null geodesics everywhere off the shock. The jump grows by $(8GE/c^4)\\ln 4$ each time $\\rho$ is divided by $4$, and a change of $\\rho_0$ moves every ray behind the shock by the same amount."],"source":{"fields":["coords","parameters","metric_components","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","domains"],"version":"991c4d44d790e96c"},"slices":[{"view":"tube","surface":0,"curve":0,"label":"$u = -1$","version":"11bf2337b00e936f","lines":[[[0.25,0.0],[1.0,0.75]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[1.0,0.75],"anchor":"br","dx":0,"dy":-1.3}},{"view":"tube","surface":0,"curve":1,"label":"$u = 0.5$","version":"39f21542b6206ed7","lines":[[[0.0,0.0],[1.0,1.0]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[0.85,0.85],"anchor":"tl","dx":1.3,"dy":1.3}},{"view":"tube","surface":0,"curve":2,"label":"$u = 1$","version":"9191a9871021d5dc","lines":[[[0.0,0.0833],[0.9167,1.0]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[0.0,0.0833],"anchor":"tl","dx":0,"dy":1.3}},{"view":"tube","surface":0,"curve":3,"label":"$u = 1.5$","version":"69117cdadb2fe439","lines":[[[0.0,0.1667],[0.8333,1.0]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[0.7083,0.875],"anchor":"br","dx":-1.3,"dy":-1.3}},{"view":"ring","surface":0,"label":"$u = -1$","ver